request.description:
**Input:** `expectedVersion` plus at least one of `orderDiscountPct` (order-level) / `lineDiscounts[]` (per line) — both can be set together, T6.4's `combineDiscounts` blends them sequentially (`1 - (1-line)*(1-order)`, NOT additive).

**Deliberately does not enforce T3.1's ceiling** — the PRD treats the ceiling as a live UI warning while drafting, not a hard save-time block; the hard check happens at Submit (T7.2).

**Output (200):**
```json
{ "lines": [
  { "...Laptop": "", "effectiveDiscountPct": "12", "netBeforeTax": "880.00", "marginPct": "20.4545" },
  { "...Setup Service": "", "effectiveDiscountPct": "18", "netBeforeTax": "164.00", "marginPct": "39.0244" }
], "summary": { "netBeforeTax": "1044.00", "marginAmount": "244.00", "marginPct": "23.3716" } }
```
Version moves to 4.

**Auth:** SALES_REP, owner, quotation must currently be `DRAFT` with >=1 line.

This is `SubmitQuotationUseCase` (T7.2): resolves each line's ceiling (T3.1), runs `scoreRisk` (T7.1) using the exact numbers already shown by T6.5, looks up the matching `ApprovalRule` (T3.2), then atomically freezes a `QuotationVersion` snapshot + persists the `RiskEvaluation` + creates `ApprovalRecord`s + transitions the quotation's status.

**Output (200) — this reproduces the TAD SS10 Gold example exactly:**
```json
{
  "quotation": { "status": "PENDING_APPROVAL", "version": 5, ... },
  "requiresApproval": true,
  "risk": {
    "score": 6.43,
    "band": "MEDIUM",
    "configVersion": 1,
    "explanation": {
      "lines": [
        { "allowedDiscountPct": 15, "effectiveDiscountPct": 12, "excessPct": 0 },
        { "allowedDiscountPct": 10, "effectiveDiscountPct": 18, "excessPct": 8 }
      ]
    }
  },
  "approvalSteps": [ { "stepOrder": 1, "role": "MANAGER" } ]
}
```
Laptop: 0 excess (compliant). Setup Service: 8 percentage points excess -> the quotation is flagged. Even though the blended `score` (~6.4) is well under the MEDIUM threshold (30) on its own, TAD SS10's override — "any line violation forces at least manager approval" — bumps the band up to MEDIUM anyway. That's why `requiresApproval` is `true` and `approvalSteps` shows the Manager step from folder 04.

**Error cases:** `400 VALIDATION_ERROR` (no lines), `409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION` (not Draft — e.g. calling this twice), `409 VERSION_CONFLICT` (stale `expectedVersion`).
